KNOWNBUG
main.i
--no-div-by-zero-check --force-malloc-success --force-realloc-success --state-hashing --add-symex-value-sets --no-align-check --k-step 2 --floatbv --unlimited-k-steps --no-vla-size-check --64  --no-por --context-bound 3 --no-pointer-check --no-bounds-check --unsigned-overflow-check --no-assertions --incremental-bmc
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
This test's VERIFICATION FAILED was an artefact of a false positive in the
unsigned shl overflow check: overflow_arith() derived signedness from either
operand, so the SHA-512 table constants `(N_UL << 32) + M_UL` (main.i:3443+)
took the signed path and were reported as overflowing for any N >= 2^31, even
though every result is representable in u64.

With that fixed, symex gets further into the file and hits a separate,
pre-existing defect:

  terminate called after throwing an instance of 'array_type2t::dyn_sized_array_excp'
    what():  Sizeof nondeterministically sized array encountered

That crash is independent of the overflow encoding -- it reproduces with
--unsigned-overflow-check removed entirely. Re-enable this test as CORE once
the dyn_sized_array_excp is fixed.
